iption>When PyMC&#39;s automatic logp derivation works for CustomDist and when it doesn&#39;t, with examples from pymc-extras including Skellam, BetaNegativeBinomial, Maxwell, and Chi.</description> <link>https://williambdean.github.io/blog/posts/2026/customdist-why-provide-logp/</link> <pubDate>Thu, 19 Nov 2026 20:46:43 +0000</pubDate> <source url="https://williambdean.github.io/feed_rss_created.xml">Will Dean</source><comments>https://williambdean.github.io/blog/posts/2026/customdist-why-provide-logp/#__comments</comments><guid isPermaLink="true">https://williambdean.github.io/blog/posts/2026/customdist-why-provide-logp/</guid> <enclosure url="https://williambdean.github.io/assets/images/social/blog/posts/2026/customdist-why-provide-logp.png" type="image/png" length="56450" /> </item> <item> <title>Predicting for New Groups in Hierarchical Models</title> <category>Bayesian Statistics</category> <category>Data Analysis</category> <category>PyMC</category> <category>Python</category> <description>How to make out-of-sample predictions for new groups in hierarchical linear models, from zero data to partial pooling, with fully reproducible PyMC code and synthetic data.</description> <link>https://williambdean.github.io/blog/posts/2026/hierarchical-group-predictions/</link> <pubDate>Thu, 19 Nov 2026 20:46:43 +0000</pubDate> <source url="https://williambdean.github.io/feed_rss_created.xml">Will Dean</source><comments>https://williambdean.github.io/blog/posts/2026/hierarchical-group-predictions/#__comments</comments><guid isPermaLink="true">https://williambdean.github.io/blog/posts/2026/hierarchical-group-predictions/</guid> <enclosure url="https://williambdean.github.io/assets/images/social/blog/posts/2026/hierarchical-group-predictions.png" type="image/png" length="53515" /> </item> <item> <title>Parallel AI Agents with Git Worktrees and uv</title> <category>Development</category> <category>Git</category> <category>GitHub Actions</category> <category>uv</category> <description>How migrating from conda to uv for speed and simplicity unlocked an unexpected benefit: clean git worktree workflows for parallel AI coding agents.</description> <link>https://williambdean.github.io/blog/posts/2026/parallel-agents-git-worktrees-uv/</link> <pubDate>Thu, 19 Nov 2026 20:46:43 +0000</pubDate> <source url="https://williambdean.github.io/feed_rss_created.xml">Will Dean</source><comments>https://williambdean.github.io/blog/posts/2026/parallel-agents-git-worktrees-uv/#__comments</comments><guid isPermaLink="true">https://williambdean.github.io/blog/posts/2026/parallel-agents-git-worktrees-uv/</guid> <enclosure url="https://williambdean.github.io/assets/images/social/blog/posts/2026/parallel-agents-git-worktrees-uv.png" type="image/png" length="57707" /> </item> <item> <title>Why Pearson φ Fails for Tweedie Pure Premiums (and How Bayesian PPC Fixes It)</title> <category>Data Analysis</category> <category>Insurance</category> <category>PyMC</category> <category>Python</category> <description>Why Pearson&#39;s chi-square dispersion estimator inflates φ by 7× for zero-inflated Tweedie pure premium models and how Bayesian posterior predictive checks fix model validation.</description> <link>https://williambdean.github.io/blog/posts/2026/pearson-phi-broken-tweedie/</link> <pubDate>Sun, 31 May 2026 23:38:31 +0000</pubDate> <source url="https://williambdean.github.io/feed_rss_created.xml">Will Dean</source><comments>https://williambdean.github.io/blog/posts/2026/pearson-phi-broken-tweedie/#__comments</comments><guid isPermaLink="true">https://williambdean.github.io/blog/posts/2026/pearson-phi-broken-tweedie/</guid> <enclosure url="https://williambdean.github.io/assets/images/social/blog/posts/2026/pearson-phi-broken-tweedie.png" type="image/png" length="60263" /> </item> <item> <title>Project-Level IPython Startup Scripts</title> <category>Config Files</category> <category>Development</category> <category>Python</category> <description>Tired of re-importing